API-14: make swmm_gage_set_rainfall() an override that the runoff step uses

swmm_gage_set_rainfall() only wrote the gage's current rainfall, which the
next runoff step recomputes from the gage's series, so the value was lost
for every gage. Also store it as the gage's API override (api_rainfall),
which updateAllGages() already applies ahead of the series and the co-gage
copy, and check that override before the co-gage in reportRainfall() too,
so that the reported rainfall of a gage that shares its series with an
earlier gage is the value set for it. The header comment now describes
how long the override lasts.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply API-14_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/include/openswmm/engine/openswmm_gages.h b/include/openswmm/engine/openswmm_gages.h
index b66bdb2..3f9d4bd 100644
--- a/include/openswmm/engine/openswmm_gages.h
+++ b/include/openswmm/engine/openswmm_gages.h
@@ -346,10 +346,12 @@ SWMM_ENGINE_API int swmm_gage_get_rain_units(SWMM_Engine engine, int idx, int* u
 SWMM_ENGINE_API int swmm_gage_get_rainfall(SWMM_Engine engine, int idx, double* rainfall);
 
 /**
- * @brief Override rainfall at a gage for the current timestep.
+ * @brief Override rainfall at a gage.
  *
  * @details Overrides gage-driven rainfall for all subcatchments that use
- *          this gage. Applied for one timestep only.
+ *          this gage, from the next runoff step until it is set again, as
+ *          legacy swmm_setValue(swmm_GAGE_RAINFALL). A negative value
+ *          returns the gage to its own rainfall data.
  */
 SWMM_ENGINE_API int swmm_gage_set_rainfall(SWMM_Engine engine, int idx, double rainfall);
 
diff --git a/src/engine/core/openswmm_gages_impl.cpp b/src/engine/core/openswmm_gages_impl.cpp
index daf90cf..9f83fde 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/openswmm_gages_impl.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/openswmm_gages_impl.cpp
@@ -355,6 +355,9 @@ SWMM_ENGINE_API int swmm_gage_set_rainfall(SWMM_Engine engine, int idx, double r
     CHECK_RUNNING(ctx);
     CHECK_INDEX(idx >= 0 && idx < ctx.n_gages());
     ctx.gages.rainfall[static_cast<std::size_t>(idx)] = rainfall;
+    // the runoff step recomputes rainfall from the gage's data unless an
+    // API override is set (legacy Gage.apiRainfall)
+    ctx.gages.api_rainfall[static_cast<std::size_t>(idx)] = rainfall;
     return SWMM_OK;
 }
 
diff --git a/src/engine/hydrology/Gage.cpp b/src/engine/hydrology/Gage.cpp
index ce8b7a1..e663963 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydrology/Gage.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydrology/Gage.cpp
@@ -401,6 +401,12 @@ static double reportRainfall(const SimulationContext& ctx, int gage_idx,
 
     auto ug = static_cast<std::size_t>(gage_idx);
 
+    // API override (legacy gage.c:544-548), checked before the co-gage as
+    // in updateAllGages
+    if (ctx.gages.api_rainfall[ug] >= 0.0) {
+        return ctx.gages.api_rainfall[ug];
+    }
+
     // Co-gage: report the primary's report rainfall re-scaled by this gage's
     // factor (legacy gage_setReportRainfall, gage.c:535-541). Co-gage index is
     // always lower than this gage's, so the recursion terminates.
@@ -414,11 +420,6 @@ static double reportRainfall(const SimulationContext& ctx, int gage_idx,
         return reportRainfall(ctx, co, report_date, from_series) * ratio;
     }
 
-    // API override (legacy gage.c:544-548)
-    if (ctx.gages.api_rainfall[ug] >= 0.0) {
-        return ctx.gages.api_rainfall[ug];
-    }
-
     // legacy gage_setReportRainfall (gage.c:550-564) on the machine's state
